Cloud Deployment Strategies

When you’re pushing new code to production, how you deploy can be the difference between a smooth release and a 2AM incident.

Here are three common deployment strategies every DevOps/Cloud Engineer should know:


🔁 1. Rolling Deployment
Upgrade in batches.
Some instances stay on the current version while others get the new one.
➡️ No downtime
➡️ Smooth transition
➡️ Can rollback midway if things go sideways

🎯 2. Canary Deployment
Like a test flight for your app.
You send a small percentage of traffic to the new version first.
✅ Safe testing in production
✅ Feedback-driven rollout
✅ Traffic ramps up only if things look good


💙💚 3. Blue-Green Deployment
Run two environments side by side.

Blue = stable, current version
Green = shiny, new version
  Once green proves itself, flip the traffic over.
  ✅ Near-zero downtime
  ✅ Easy rollback
  ✅ Requires a bit more infra, but worth it for critical apps

Different teams use different strategies based on their risk tolerance, infra setup, and business impact.
